s" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064407 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186065139 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064407 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064407 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ec92f9e5-f4ff-5e7d-bf06-75063f0fdeca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065139 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065139 #edb/ref 1061 1966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065139 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3d1d4c5b-f669-5ef8-ae3a-069d89747d69" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065139 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065140 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065140 #edb/ref 1061 1967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065140 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0b4e1339-dcb7-5439-a531-66ef32ae8045" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065140 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065141 #edb/ref 1061 1971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065141 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "91fabaf9-366a-5699-bd24-1f3331ce4790" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065141 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065178 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065178 #edb/ref 1061 27313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065178 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "55aedc57-c528-5f39-b05b-126f9ef5cee0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065178 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065333 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's find the total area of the finite region enclosed between curves the curves\n\n$$\nf(x)=x^3-2x\n$$\n\nand $g(x)=2x$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e6/e651f9df1fbc9f0f9ad8ffa49822e4e3640a3555570ca3d0f82c155c5141843e.png)\n\nFirst, we find the points where the curves intersect:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= g(x) \\\\\nx^{3} - 2x &= 2x \\\\\nx^{3} - 4x &= 0 \\\\\nx(x^{2} - 4) &= 0 \\\\\nx(x - 2)(x + 2) &= 0 \\\\\nx &= 0, 2,-2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area we want consists of two symmetric regions: $A_1$ and $A_2$.\n\n![](images/4f/4fd6173127725bd771a753217002ab9656cf36a97dd37c4fe80f7d76e672ee86.png)\n\nFor the area $A_1$, we have $x \\in [-2,0]$, and the upper function is $f(x)$ while the lower function is $g(x)$. So, the area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{1} &= \\int_{-2}^{0}(f(x) - g(x))dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{-2}^{0}((x^{3} - 2x) - 2x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{-2}^{0}(x^{3} - 4x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{-2}^{0}x^{3}dx - 4\\int_{-2}^{0}xdx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{x^{4}}{4}\\right|_{-2}^{0} - 4 \\cdot \\left.\\frac{x^{2}}{2}\\right|_{-2}^{0} \\\\\n&= (0 - 4) - 4(0 - 2) \\\\\n&=-4 + 8 \\\\\n&= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the regions are symmetric, we have that $A_2=A_1=4$.\n\nFinally, the required area is given by\n\n$$\nA = A_1 + A_2 = 4 + 4 = 8\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065333 #edb/ref 1065 1003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065333 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "988c723b-81d1-541c-9ab3-bebbece1cf06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065333 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
